-- MTH 121 (Elementary Mathematics II, UNN) practice questions for the CBT feature.
-- Source: real worked calculus questions supplied by the user (functions, limits,
-- continuity, differentiation, integration). One question was dropped: the definite
-- integral of 1/[(x-1)(x+2)] from 0 to 1 has a singularity at x=1 (the upper bound),
-- so it diverges and none of the supplied answer choices are mathematically valid.
--
-- cbt_questions has no course_code column, so the MTH 121 link lives in subject_name.
-- is_general = true so every student sees this paper regardless of faculty, since
-- MTH 121 is a shared 100-level requirement across several science/engineering
-- departments, not exclusive to Mathematics majors.

delete from public.cbt_questions where subject_id = 'mth-121-calculus';

